{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.IwahoriHecke.TwFromMatsumoto","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.TwFromMatsumoto","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.IwahoriHecke.BraidWordInvariance","lean:module:Mathlib.GroupTheory.Coxeter.Length"],"declarations":8,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.TwMatsumoto.Tw_one_of_matsumoto","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.TwMatsumoto.Tw_one_of_matsumoto","kind":"theorem","line":131,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/TwFromMatsumoto.lean#L131-L139","doc":"The identity has `T_1 = 1`: the chosen reduced word for `1` is empty, since it is reduced and\n`ℓ(1) = 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.TwMatsumoto.exists_Tw_of_matsumoto","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.TwMatsumoto.exists_Tw_of_matsumoto","kind":"theorem","line":113,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/TwFromMatsumoto.lean#L113-L129","doc":"**`T_w` exists as soon as Matsumoto does — the satisfiable form.**\n\nThe hypothesis is Matsumoto's theorem verbatim: two **reduced** words with the same image in `W`\nare braid-equivalent. The conclusion is a `Tw : W → H(M, q)` agreeing with the word product on\nevery **reduced** word, which is what the `T_w` basis means.\n\nContrast `exists_Tw_of_braidEquiv`, whose all-words hypothesis is refuted above. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.TwMatsumoto.wordProd_redWord","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.TwMatsumoto.wordProd_redWord","kind":"theorem","line":108,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/TwFromMatsumoto.lean#L108-L109","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.TwMatsumoto.redWord_isReduced","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.TwMatsumoto.redWord_isReduced","kind":"theorem","line":105,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/TwFromMatsumoto.lean#L105-L106","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.TwMatsumoto.redWord","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.TwMatsumoto.redWord","kind":"def","line":102,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/TwFromMatsumoto.lean#L102-L103","doc":"A chosen reduced word for each element. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.TwMatsumoto.not_braidEquiv_hypothesis","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.TwMatsumoto.not_braidEquiv_hypothesis","kind":"theorem","line":84,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/TwFromMatsumoto.lean#L84-L98","doc":"🛑 **The all-words hypothesis is false for `cs.wordProd`.**\n\n`π [i,i] = π []` because `s_i² = 1`, but braid-equivalence preserves length and `2 ≠ 0`. So\n`exists_Tw_of_braidEquiv`, instantiated at the word product of a Coxeter system — the only\ninstantiation it exists for — has a hypothesis nothing can discharge, and proves nothing.\n\nStated for the Coxeter matrix's own entries, which are symmetric by `CoxeterMatrix.symmetric`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.TwMatsumoto.braidEquiv_length_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.TwMatsumoto.braidEquiv_length_eq","kind":"theorem","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/TwFromMatsumoto.lean#L73-L78","doc":"**Braid-equivalence preserves word length.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.TwMatsumoto.braidMove_length_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.TwMatsumoto.braidMove_length_eq","kind":"theorem","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/TwFromMatsumoto.lean#L64-L71","doc":"A single braid move preserves word length, when `M` is symmetric — which it is for a Coxeter\nmatrix. The two alternating blocks have lengths `M i j` and `M j i`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}